### Concrete source progress — 2026-11-10

Normal startup now creates `SimpleATHInfraProtocol` and calls native Infra/
Skywalk initialization, attach/start/publication and native packet registration.
`TahoePacketPath` owns real pool/queue factories, count-based TX/RX callbacks,
completion and pressure; no fake Ethernet provider wrapper is used. Modern
scan/abort/result/done and inventory/MAC/power/link paths are production callers
of the physical-owner contract. A command gate and timer serialize mailboxes;
stop cancels work before provider/queue lifetime ends. See the design record
for exact static evidence and remaining ABI assumptions.

Strict syntax-only SDK checks passed for 3 changed native translation units;
the production scan codec's host fixture passed. Nineteen native method labels
were verified as defined external symbols in the exact KDK. These checks do
not prove loading, packet registration or RF success. The source progress
below supersedes the initially missing native join/PMK and capability paths;
remaining native operations, AWDL and physical RF activation still keep this
TODO open.

### Integrated WCL join and card inventory follow-through

`78b2aa7` and subsequent native fixes connect version-2 epoch/request-scoped
PMK delivery to the physical driver's real selection/authentication path.
The native child now posts association, first-beacon, supplicant, connection,
abort and loss events only from matching observed provider state, with bounded
timeout and copied BSS/signal metadata. These are normal target callers,
not standalone codecs. Safe EDMA key-update work is separately integrated;
this record does not claim end-to-end WPA2 or packet operation without the
remaining RF startup and native transport work.

The controller's previously unconditional Unsupported card-capability response
is replaced with a complete 0x1c native envelope: CCMP/WPA2, short timing and
asynchronous scan/completion inventory. KDK `setCardCapbilities` at 0xf04fc
copies exactly 28 bytes; the compatibility SDK's legacy structure is only 16.
Exact later feature-byte readers were checked before zeroing unsupported
bands/HE/EHT rather than copying a different chipset's bitmap. The new normal
controller uses `TahoeCapabilities.hpp`, covered by an offline wire-layout
fixture and strict SDK C++14 syntax. Full lint and runtime proof are separate.

